e  british success at the glorious world  sports awards tennis player emma  radakani won breakthrough of the year  award skateboarder skye brown took home  the comeback of the year award she  recovered from an injury didn't she and  bmx rider bethany shriver won the action  sports person award nice one guys  here at fyi we aim to give you a voice  with big conversations on big issues we  call it conversation  this month marks two years since the  global black lives matter protest  against racism and fyi's declan met  singer keijin bryant  this is their conversation  [Music]  i'm a young black man  [Music]  doing all that i can  in may 2020 12 year old singer kedren  bryant posted a video on social media  it went viral  [Music]  i just wanna live  the song i just wanna live which he had  written with his mother was inspired by  kedran's fear of being killed  because he is black  i just wanna leave  [Music]  i'm a young black man  it was shared by the former us president  barack obama beyonce will smith william  and many more famous black americans  it was the height of the global reaction  to the murder of the african-american  george floyd by a white police officer  his death was seen as another example of  terrible racism not just among some  police officers but across  society me as a young black man in  america it was just enlightening it just  gave me hope to keep going on and keep  spreading the message keep fighting for  what is right  the world felt that enough was enough it  was just no longer acceptable that  someone young and talented could fear  for their future in america or anywhere  in the world simply because of their  color  but two years on from george floyd's  death i want to know has anything really  changed  [Music]  i'm in jacksonville the biggest city in  the state of florida in the usa where  kedran brian and nearly 300 000 black  americans live  what i do know is that since the black  lives matter protests the lives of  kedron and his family 